          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On September 1, 1978, at 21:05, three members of the same family observed a red glow moving slowly across the sky between Mont Saint-Michel and Mont Angel. The observation lasted two to three minutes. No further observations were made by the gendarmes contacted immediately by phone. No other testimony regarding this phenomenon, for which we have limited information, was collected.",
